@                           vxitedit
                          ---------

VXI Text Resource Editor (vxitedit) is an interactive program that
incorporates several resource editors and displays such as:

Resource Manager Display: Use this display to view the Resource
Manager table information.

Configuration Editor:  Use this editor to configure the VXIbus 
interface hardware.

Manufacturer Name Editor: Use this editor to update the list of 
manufacturer names and numbers.

Model Name Editor: Use this editor to update the list of model
names, manufacturer names and model numbers.

Device Name Editor: Use this editor to update the list of VXI
devices in the system.

Non-VXI Device Name Editor: Use this editor to update the list of
non-VXI devices.

Interrupt Configuration Editor: Use this editor to define individual
and intra-mainframe interrupt configurations.

Trigger Configuration Editor: Use this editor to define intra-
mainframe trigger configurations.

Utility Bus Configuration Editor: Use this editor to define utility
bus configurations.

Using vxitedit
--------------
vxitedit is a text-based program. It supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the 
				      specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) add                           - lets you add an entry.
(4) duplicate   <index#>          - lets you duplicate an entry.
(5) modify	<index#>,<field#> - lets you modify an existing entry.
(6) delete	<index#>	  - lets you delete an entry.
(7) show	<field#>	  - shows information about the field.
(8) save			  - lets you save the information.
(9) abort			  - lets you exit the editor, 
				    ignoring the changes made.
(10) exit			  - lets you exit the editor.
(11) help			  - gives help on that editor.

NUMBERS can be entered in vxitedit as:

	50	-	decimal 50
	0x50	-	hex	50

Note:  All the numbers displayed in vxitedit except index# and field#
-----  are in hex.

HELP
----
You can obtain help on any editor by typing 'help'


